547	    // even with it; pre-existing merges already on the base are out of range.
548	    //
549	    // The range alone trusts the merge-base to be right, and it isn't always: a
550	    // shallow clone's grafted boundary or a criss-cross history can hand back a
551	    // merge-base that sweeps the base branch's own merges into the range. So each
552	    // candidate is confirmed against the base ref itself — a merge already on the
553	    // base branch was never introduced here, whatever the range says. Offline and
